---
import SiteLayout from '../components/SiteLayout.astro';
import SoftCta from '../components/SoftCta.astro';
---

<SiteLayout
  title="About Jacob Vermeulen — Songdance"
  description="Jacob Vermeulen — pianist, singer, and educator, and the person behind Somatic Vocal Healing. He holds space; people heal themselves."
>
  <header class="sd-section sd-about-hero">
    <div class="sd-about-hero-inner">
      <figure class="sd-about-portrait">
        <img src="/media/library/jacob-tree.png" alt="Jacob Vermeulen" />
      </figure>
      <div class="sd-about-intro" data-anim="reveal">
        <div class="sd-eyebrow">About</div>
        <h1 class="sd-pagehero-title">Jacob Vermeulen</h1>
        <p class="sd-pagehero-lede">
          Pianist, singer, and educator. The person behind Somatic Vocal Healing.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </header>

  <section class="sd-section sd-prose">
    <div class="sd-prose-inner">
      <p>
        I started with singing. For the better part of twenty years I taught authentic singing
        — holidays, workshops, retreats — fascinated less by technique than by something
        underneath it: change how a person <em>feels</em>, and the voice changes on its own. The
        reverse turned out to be true too. That was the thread I kept pulling.
      </p>
      <p>
        Then life did what life does, and my focus moved from singing to sounding. Not the voice
        that reaches for a beautiful note — the voice that tells the truth about what’s happening
        inside, in this exact moment. Out of that, over years and a great many sessions, Somatic
        Vocal Healing took shape.
      </p>
      <p>
        I don’t think of myself as a healer. I hold space; people heal themselves. My job is to
        make that safe and possible, and then to get out of the way. I’ve had the privilege of
        doing this with thousands of people across Europe and South Africa, online and in person
        — and I’m still learning what the voice can do.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="sd-section sd-about-quote">
    <p class="t-lyric sd-about-quote-text">
      “You can’t heal and understand at the same time. So we begin with the experience.”
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="sd-section sd-prose">
    <div class="sd-prose-inner">
      <p class="sd-about-facts">
        Jacob lives in Belgium with his partner, Lieselot. He works in English; the
        German-language practice is led by <strong>Carmen &amp; Lorenz</strong>, and he
        collaborates with <strong>Karen Evans</strong>, <strong>Daniela Hess</strong>, and
        <strong>Lesanne</strong> across courses and retreats. He is currently writing his first
        book, <em>Healing, Honestly.</em>
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <SoftCta
    text="Curious how this actually feels?"
    ctaLabel="Sit in on a live session — 9€"
    ctaHref="/session"
    altLabel="What is SVH? →"
    altHref="/what-is-svh"
  />
</SiteLayout>
